error[E0277]: `OpaqueBlob<Unwiped>` cannot be decrypted from one `Ciphertext`
  --> tests/ui/opaque_blob_requires_zeroize.rs:18:48
   |
18 |     let _refused: OpaqueBlob<Unwiped> = keyset.decrypt(ct).await.unwrap();
   |                                                ^^^^^^^ one `Ciphertext` decrypts into one owned value
   |
   = help: the trait `OpaqueDecode` is not implemented for `OpaqueBlob<Unwiped>`
   = note: one value is a scalar, such as a `String`, a `bool`, a float, a `Vec<u8>`, or a fixed-width integer other than `u8`. The docs of `OpaqueDecode` list every type that is accepted.
   = note: an `Option` or a `Protected` of a scalar is one value too. So is a newtype that derives `Decrypt` over a scalar.
   = note: for a date, a timestamp, a decimal, or a UUID, use `value::Date`, `value::Timestamp`, `value::Decimal`, or `value::Uuid`. A `uuid::Uuid`, a `rust_decimal::Decimal`, and the jiff types do not implement `Zeroize`.
   = note: the type must also implement `Zeroize`, so that a decrypted value can be wiped when a later decrypt in the same call fails.
   = note: the type must also be `Send` and `'static`. A `'static` type borrows no data.
   = note: to decrypt a `Vec<Ciphertext>` into a `Vec`, with one element from each `Ciphertext`, use `DecryptFrom`.
   = note: to decrypt a sequence, a map, or a struct that derives `Decrypt`, use `keyset.decrypt_tree`. `keyset.encrypt_tree` makes the tree of ciphertexts that it reads.
   = note: to decrypt a whole `Deserialize` value from one `Ciphertext`, decrypt into `OpaqueBlob<T>`. `T` must also implement `Default` and `Zeroize`.
help: the trait `OpaqueDecode` is implemented for `OpaqueBlob<T>`
  --> src/blob.rs
